9. GRAVITY EXPERIMENT
======================================================================

The primary experiment evaluates six predefined gravitational conditions:

G01 = 1.00 g
G02 = 0.75 g
G03 = 0.50 g
G04 = 0.38 g
G05 = 0.16 g
G06 = 0.00 g

The gravity axis is conventionally ordered:

1.00 g
    ->
0.75 g
    ->
0.50 g
    ->
0.38 g
    ->
0.16 g
    ->
0.00 g

This corresponds to progressively reduced gravitational loading from
terrestrial conditions toward microgravity.

For the primary gravity sweep, the baseline patient-specific geometry,
mesh, fiber representation, material formulation, and numerical
configuration are intended to remain fixed unless explicitly identified
as a gravity-dependent input.

Gravity is introduced through the predefined gravitational body-force
condition / gravity multiplier.

The controlled experimental design is therefore:

5 patient-specific subjects
×
6 gravity conditions

=
30 planned subject × gravity combinations.

Execution status of the individual combinations is controlled separately
by:

07_Simulation_Execution/
Simulation_Execution_Evidence_Registry.txt

