15. INTERPRETATION OF THE RECOVERED GRAVITY RESPONSE
======================================================================

The recovered numerical pattern indicates that progressive reduction in
gravity is associated with lower modeled:

- peak myocardial von Mises stress
- peak principal strain
- maximum ventricular displacement
- ventricular strain energy

while the modeled LV cavity volume shows a small increase across the
gravity sequence.

The principal qualitative response pattern is therefore:

Reduced gravity
    ->
Reduced modeled mechanical loading
    ->
Reduced stress / strain / displacement
    ->
Reduced strain energy

with a comparatively small increase in modeled LV cavity volume.

This interpretation is restricted to the modeled solid-mechanics response.

It must not be interpreted as direct prediction of systemic
cardiovascular adaptation, blood-flow redistribution, autonomic
adaptation, or chronic physiological remodeling.

