26. PROHIBITED RECONSTRUCTION PRACTICES
======================================================================

The following are prohibited:

1. Inventing missing COMSOL outputs.

2. Back-calculating patient-level values from group means.

3. Creating artificial historical solver logs.

4. Assigning "verified" status based only on a figure.

5. Treating a reported value as proof of execution.

6. Changing numerical values to improve agreement between figures and
   tables.

7. Reconstructing undocumented model parameters solely to reproduce a
   desired result.

8. Describing external reference comparisons as independent validation
   without establishing the calibration/validation relationship.

9. Representing planned simulations as completed simulations.

10. Representing a reconstructed computational workflow as historical
    execution unless the evidence supports that statement.

