28. FINAL COMPUTATIONAL SCOPE STATEMENT
======================================================================

The definitive computational model is a patient-specific ventricular
finite-element solid-mechanics model used to investigate the mechanical
response of cardiac tissue under six predefined gravitational loading
conditions.

The principal modeled response variables are myocardial stress,
myocardial strain, ventricular displacement, LV cavity volume, and
ventricular strain energy.

The recovered Figure 6 dataset demonstrates a consistent modeled
reduction in stress, strain, displacement, and strain energy with
progressive reduction in gravity, together with a small increase in
modeled LV cavity volume.

These findings describe the behavior of the computational model under
the specified loading conditions.

They should not be interpreted as direct evidence of systemic
cardiovascular adaptation in humans without additional physiological
validation.

